  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNHCR Winterization Plan in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Earmarked support for UNHCR&apos;s Winterization Plan, as part of the UN Winter Response Plan for Ukraine (October 2023-March 2024) coordinated by OCHA. UNHCR&apos;s winterization plan aims to reach 900,000 individual during the 2023-2024 winter season, including through cash support for winter energy needs, shelter and housing assistance (incl. rental market suport, insulation support and provision of heaters), winterized non-food item kits, winter clothing, provision of generators, and collective site management and winter preparation support to collective sites.

Gender equality and protection is at the centre of the UN Winter Response Plan for Ukraine, as is also the case for the overarching 2023 Humanitarian Response Plan. Humanitarian partners commit to enhance accountibility to affected people (AAP), prevent sexual exploitation and abuse (PSEA) , increase information and communication about conflict-related sexual violence and human trafficking, ensure the response is gender-and age-sensitive, and promote protection through all aspects of humanitarian programmes and advocacy. The reporting requires data disaggregated by sex, age, and disability. The inclusion of people with disabilities is integrated across project activities.</narrative>
  </description>
